SUMMARY:Stories on Stage Davis
DESCRIPTION:Naomi Williams\, author of the novel Landfalls\, long-listed for the Center for Fiction First Novel Prize and former Director of Stories on Stage Davis and actor Sara Matsui-Colby will be presenting a reading of “Dead Astronauts”—about nine-year-old Hana lives in Long Beach\, California\, in 1972\, in a family she already understands is strange — a white father who speaks perfect Japanese\, a Japanese mother who won’t step onto the balcony without her outside shoes\, a religion that keeps detailed records on who will burn forever and who will not.\nJeri Howitt\, Founder and Director of Stories on Stage Davis from 2013-2016\, and returning to the Director position for Season XII and Tim Gaffaney\, Director of Casting for Stories on Stage Davis will present a reading of a story called “Escape\, Escape\, Escape”—a psychological suspense piece with a light\, almost playful touch — until suddenly isn’t. This is a story that will stay with you\, and that performs beautifully\, because so much of what it’s about is the unreliability of the voice telling it. Storiesonstagedavis.com \n 
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/stories-on-stage-davis/
LOCATION:Sudwerk Brewing Co  2001 2nd Street  Davis\, CA 95618\, 2001 2nd Street\, Davis\, CA\, 95618\, United States
